#!/bin/bash
# post-commit: intentionally a no-op.
#
# This hook USED to auto-bump package.json version, rewrite CHANGELOG.md, create a
# release commit, and tag on EVERY commit on EVERY branch. That behaviour is
# incompatible with a deliberately-versioned release process:
#   - it fought the single source of truth (package.json feeds src/version.ts),
#   - it coupled the version number to commit cadence rather than release decisions,
#   - it produced nonsense history (e.g. 1.9.0 and 1.10.0 sharing a date).
#
# Versioning is now done by hand: bump package.json, hand-write the CHANGELOG entry,
# and tag `vX.Y.Z` explicitly when cutting a release. See WS-D5 in the release plan.
#
# The file is kept (not deleted) so `git config core.hooksPath .hooks` has a valid,
# executable hook and nothing errors. Do not reintroduce auto-bumping here.
exit 0
